    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-15T04:11:16+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-15T04:11:16+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-14T18:41:16Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-14T18:41:16Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred in the Bight, is slowly drifting to the southeast to be located in the Tasman Sea on Monday. A ridge of high pressure is expected to remain over South Australia. A trough over QLD pushes into the far northeast of SA from later Saturday through to later Monday. A trough of low pressure moves in the far west of South Australia later on Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-15T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-14T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. High chance of showers north of Marla, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Marla this morning. Winds easterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures between 15 and 19.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:10am to 3:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. Light winds becoming east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning then becoming light in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers south of Woomera, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Stuart Highway in the afternoon. Light winds becoming northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 22.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-19T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-18T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers south of Woomera, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm south of Coober Pedy in the afternoon. Winds northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly during the day then decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 27.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
